        <section id="section-lessons" data-route="lessons">
            <h3>Private Music Production & Mixing Lessons</h3>
            <p>One-on-one, project-based lessons for high-school students, aspiring college audio majors, independent artists, and adult learners in Nashville.</p>
            <p>My goal is to help students understand what they are hearing, use their tools intentionally, and build a creative process they can eventually carry on without me.</p>
            <p><a class="button-link" href="#lessons" onclick="document.getElementById('lessons-inquiry').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' }); return false;">Request a Consultation</a></p>

            <h3>Who I Teach</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width: 35%;">Student</th>
                        <th>Focus</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {% for audience in lessons.audiences %}
                    <tr>
                        <td><div class="lesson-heading">{{ audience.label | safe }}</div></td>
                        <td>{{ audience.focus | safe }}</td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p>Complete beginners are welcome. Students do not need to play an instrument or already own professional equipment.</p>

            <h3>What We Can Work On</h3>
            <ul class="lesson-list">
                {% for topic in lessons.topics %}
                <li>{{ topic | safe }}</li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            <p>Lessons stay within my professional experience in recording, production, mixing, and studio workflow. If a student needs advanced help outside that lane, I will be honest about the boundary and recommend a specialist when possible.</p>

            <h3>How Lessons Work</h3>
            <p>We start with a free 20-minute phone or video consultation and a short intake form. The first lesson includes an informal assessment and a practical hands-on activity.</p>
            <p>From there, we build a learning direction around essential audio concepts and a real project or clearly defined goal. Students operate the DAW for most of the lesson; my job is to demonstrate, guide, ask useful questions, and help them understand their choices.</p>

            <h3>Lesson Options</h3>
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width: 35%;">Option</th>
                        <th>Best For</th>
                        <th style="width: 20%;">Rate</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {% for option in lessons.lessonOptions %}
                    <tr>
                        <td><div class="lesson-heading">{{ option.label | safe }}</div></td>
                        <td>{{ option.bestFor | safe }}</td>
                        <td>{{ option.rate | safe }}</td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p>Lessons are offered one-on-one and by appointment.</p>

            <h3>The Studio</h3>
            <p>In-person lessons take place in a detached, finished private studio at my residential property in East Nashville. The exact address and arrival instructions are provided after enrollment and appointment confirmation.</p>
            <ul>
                {% for feature in lessons.studioFeatures %}
                <li>{{ feature | safe }}</li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            <div class="lesson-photo-placeholder">Studio photo placeholder</div>
            <p>Cats live on the property but are kept outside the studio during lessons. Please mention any significant animal allergies before scheduling.</p>

            <h3>For Parents</h3>
            <p>Parents and guardians are welcome to observe lessons. Students under 16 must have a parent or authorized adult remain on the property.</p>
            <ul>
                {% for policy in lessons.parentPolicies %}
                <li>{{ policy | safe }}</li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            <p>The studio is maintained as a professional, substance-free learning environment with clear safety, hearing-protection, and conduct policies.</p>

            <h3>FAQ</h3>
            {% for faq in lessons.faqs %}
            <div class="lesson-faq-item">
                <div class="lesson-heading">{{ faq.question | safe }}</div>
                <p>{{ faq.answer | safe }}</p>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}

            <h3 id="lessons-inquiry">Request a Consultation</h3>
            <p>The first step is a free 20-minute phone or video consultation. Submitting an inquiry does not commit you to purchasing lessons.</p>
            <form action="https://formspree.io/f/xjgznrlq" method="POST" class="contact-form">
                <input type="hidden" name="inquiry_type" value="Lessons consultation">
                <p><label>Name: <br><input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required /></label></p>
                <p><label>Email: <br><input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required /></label></p>
                <p><label>Student age, experience, and goals: <br><textarea name="message" rows="5" required></textarea></label></p>
                <p><button type="submit">Send Inquiry</button></p>
            </form>
        </section>
